      "label": "FactSet-style public evidence workflow",
      "classes": "cream evidence-slide",
      "body": "<div class=\"header-row\"><h2>Start with evidence: what dividend and earnings will we value?</h2></div><div class=\"rule\"></div>\n<div class=\"evidence-purpose\">A valuation formula needs a clearly defined input. These two figures answer different questions.</div>\n<div class=\"factset-console\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Public-data teaching mockup links Coca-Cola's annualized 2026 dividend of 2.12 to dividend valuation and FY2025 diluted GAAP EPS of 3.04 to a trailing P E cross-check\"><div class=\"console-top\"><strong>KO · The Coca-Cola Company</strong><span>FACTSET WORKFLOW MOCKUP · public data only</span></div><div class=\"console-grid\"><b>Public evidence</b><b>Recorded value</b><b>How we will use it</b><span>Annualized 2026 dividend</span><strong>$2.12 per share</strong><small>Cash paid to owners → dividend model</small><span>FY2025 diluted GAAP EPS</span><strong>$3.04 per share</strong><small>Accounting earnings → trailing P/E cross-check</small><span>Public source</span><strong>Coca-Cola 2025 Form 10-K</strong><small>Different periods; keep the labels attached</small></div></div>\n<div class=\"evidence-purpose-check\"><strong>Check before calculating</strong><p>Is it a dividend or EPS? Historical or expected? Annual or quarterly? A per-share figure or a company total?</p></div>\n<div class=\"evidence-pipeline\"><span>Field</span><i>→</i><span>Definition</span><i>→</i><span>Period</span><i>→</i><span>Units</span><i>→</i><span>Currency</span><i>→</i><span>Supplier</span><i>→</i><span>Retrieval date</span></div>\n<a class=\"source-link\" href=\"https://investors.coca-colacompany.com/filings-reports/annual-filings-10-k/content/0001628280-26-010047/ko-20251231.htm\">Public source: Coca-Cola 2025 Form 10-K · USD/share · supplier: Coca-Cola IR / SEC</a>",
      "note": "Purpose: establish the two public inputs students will use later and prevent input-definition mistakes before calculation. Read the dividend row as cash distributions per share; read EPS as accounting income per share, not cash available to shareholders. Ask which figure belongs in a dividend model and which belongs in a trailing earnings multiple. The annualized 2026 dividend is 2.12 dollars while diluted GAAP EPS is FY2025 at 3.04 dollars, so the periods are explicitly different. In the Gordon example treat 2.12 as D1 from a beginning-of-2026 teaching valuation date; it is not a rolling forward forecast today. The 8.5 percent required return, 4 percent growth, and 22-times multiple are separate classroom assumptions, not facts in this evidence table. Students should record field, definition, period, units, currency, supplier and their own retrieval date when sourcing a fresh input. Do not teach this mockup as a live FactSet screen. Time: 2 minutes."
