      "note": "Post debt is 100 million; post book equity is 645 million. Cash stays 45 million because all 400 million proceeds have been used. Assets become 830 million and liabilities are 185 million, giving a tied balance sheet. Short-term debt falls from 60 to zero, so current liabilities fall from 145 to 85 million and the current ratio improves even though cash is unchanged. Interest falls from 36 to 12 million, after-tax income rises from 164.25 to 182.25 million, coverage rises from 7.08 to 21.25, D/E falls from 1.22 to 0.16, and simplified ending-equity ROE falls from 67.0 to 28.3 percent. These are year-one pro forma earnings with no incremental capex earnings yet. Time: 3 minutes."
