      "body": "\n<img class=\"revision-backdrop\" src=\"assets/valuation-hero.webp\" alt=\"Analyst reviewing financial evidence and valuation assumptions\"><div class=\"header-row\"><h2>Will higher total earnings protect EPS?</h2></div><div class=\"rule\"></div><div class=\"dilution-setup\"><div><span>Before the offering</span><strong>$164.25M income</strong><p>50M existing shares</p></div><i>→</i><div><span>After Scenario C</span><strong>$182.25M income</strong><p>50M existing + 20M new shares</p></div></div><div class=\"formula-pair\"><code>EPS = net income / shares</code><code>Ownership = holder shares / total shares</code></div><div class=\"deliverable\">Founder owns 20M shares and sells none. Deliver: pre/post EPS, founder ownership, and income needed to hold EPS.</div>\n    ",
